lax fork patch for ReflowTeX — marker capture in the node-list serializer.

SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
Derived from: https://github.com/radek-p/reflowtex @ 36f8365eed25ece1db38e0059bcbba3c250802e1
              (src/extract/serializer.lua, AGPL-3.0-or-later)

The three capture sites the stage-0 spike validated (spike/paper/reflow/
REPORT.md), productionized verbatim in shape:
  1. a \laxmark whatsit *inside a paragraph* becomes a {type="marker"}
     node at its exact node-list position;
  2. a whatsit in the *shipout walk* (vertical mode, between line boxes and
     displays) becomes a {kind="marker"} content-stream item — stock code
     has no whatsit branch there and silently drops all of them;
  3. markers trapped in *glyphless resumed paragraphs* (an end marker
     directly after \end{equation}, then a blank line) are hoisted into
     the stream — the walk skips such captures entirely.
Plus last_flow(): the walk's display-spacing questions ("what did the
stream just emit") look through trailing marker items, so markers never
perturb below/abovedisplayskip restoration.
And has_ink (was upstream's has_glyphs): the walk's body gate counts
pictures as ink, because a paragraph that is only an externalised
tikzpicture bears no glyph at any depth — the glyph-only gate (upstream
has the same one) silently drops every standalone figure from the content
stream. Captures with neither glyphs nor pictures still take the
marker-hoist branch (site 3).

Marker identity: user_defined whatsit, user_id 90210, string value
"b:<n>" / "e:<n>" (laxreflow.sty is the writer; ids never enter the list).

